# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks files out as CRLF by default, and two
# test files parse src/App.tsx with patterns like /\n  \{\n/ to find the SCENES
# table. A CRLF checkout puts \r before every \n, those patterns match nothing,
# and four tests fail claiming there are no gated scenes.
#
# The failure is invisible where it is usually looked for. CI runs on Linux and
# checks out LF, so the suite is green on every push while being unrunnable for
# anyone developing on Windows — the platform this application also ships to.
# Pinning eol here means the working tree matches CI on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or they will not execute; the build scripts are
# invoked directly by scripts/build-editions.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Batch files are the one exception: cmd.exe requires CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.dmg  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
